### Bước 1: Pre-Review Gate(s) — TRƯỚC KHI VIẾT CODE

Output header:
```
══════════════════════════════════════
[PRE-REVIEW GATE]
══════════════════════════════════════
```

**Với mỗi skill được activate, chạy đầy đủ pre-review checklist của skill đó:**

#### A. frontend-taste Pre-Review (Section 0.A - 0.F)

**0.A Brief Inference:**
- [ ] Page kind: landing (SaaS/consumer/agency/event), portfolio, redesign, editorial
- [ ] Vibe words: aesthetic direction keywords
- [ ] Reference signals: URLs, screenshots, named products/brands
- [ ] Audience: ai sẽ xem (procurement panel, consumer, recruiter)
- [ ] Brand assets: logo, color, type, photography có sẵn
- [ ] Quiet constraints: accessibility-first, public-sector, regulated industries

**0.B Design Read Declaration (bắt buộc, 1 dòng):**
```
"Reading this as: [B2B SaaS landing] for [technical buyers], 
 with a [Linear-style minimalist] language, 
 leaning toward [Tailwind + Geist + restrained motion]."
```
- [ ] Design read declared (verbatim, không được phép suy ra sau khi code)

**0.C Ambiguous Brief Protocol:**
- [ ] Nếu brief ambiguous → hỏi đúng 1 câu hỏi làm rõ, không đoán

**0.D Anti-Default Discipline:**
- [ ] Không có AI-purple gradients / centered hero over dark mesh trong plan
- [ ] Không có Three equal feature cards / generic glassmorphism trong plan
- [ ] Không có Inter + slate-900 / infinite-loop micro-animations trong plan
- [ ] Nếu có → loại bỏ trước khi proceed

**0.E Design System Check:**
- [ ] Brief có match official design system không? Nếu có → dùng official package
  - Microsoft/enterprise → `@fluentui/react-components`
  - Google/Material → `@material/web`
  - IBM/B2B → `@carbon/react`
  - Shopify → `polaris.js`
  - Modern SaaS → `shadcn/ui`
  - Modern accessible → `@radix-ui/themes`
  - Modern SaaS/AI → Tailwind v4 + `dark:` variant

**0.F Pre-Code Review Checklist (PASS GATE):**
- [ ] Design read declared (Section 0.B) ✓
- [ ] No AI-default patterns in draft plan (0.D checked) ✓
- [ ] Design system selected if applicable (0.E) ✓
- [ ] Dial values set: VARIANCE (1-10), MOTION (1-10), DENSITY (1-10) ✓
- [ ] Hero plan fits viewport (headline max 2 lines, subtext max 20 words) ✓
- [ ] Section layout diversity planned (no 3+ consecutive same-layout sections) ✓

#### B. frontend-redesign Pre-Review (Section 0.A - 0.E)

**0.A Scan the Codebase:**
- [ ] Framework identified (React/Vue/Next.js/Nuxt/vanilla)
- [ ] Styling method identified (Tailwind/CSS modules/styled-components/vanilla CSS)
- [ ] Current design patterns and component structure documented
- [ ] `package.json` dependencies checked
- [ ] Tailwind version checked (v3 vs v4) before modifying config

**0.B Audit the Current State:**
- [ ] Brand tokens: primary/accent colors, type stack, logo treatment, radii
- [ ] Information architecture: page tree, primary nav, conversion paths
- [ ] Content blocks: what exists, what's working, what's filler
- [ ] Patterns to preserve: signature interactions, recognizable hero, copy voice
- [ ] Patterns to retire: AI-slop tells, broken layouts, dead links, generic imagery
- [ ] Dial reading: infer VARIANCE/MOTION/DENSITY of existing site
- [ ] SEO baseline: ranking pages, meta titles, structured data, OG cards

**0.C Classify Redesign Mode:**
- [ ] **Preserve** — modernize without breaking brand → extract tokens first
- [ ] **Overhaul** — new visual language on top of existing content → visuals greenfield, preserve content/IA

**0.D Pre-Redesign Review Checklist (PASS GATE):**
- [ ] Framework and styling method identified ✓
- [ ] Existing brand tokens extracted ✓
- [ ] Redesign mode classified ✓
- [ ] SEO baseline documented ✓
- [ ] Accessibility baseline noted ✓
- [ ] Analytics dependencies identified ✓
- [ ] Dial reading performed ✓

**0.E What Never Changes Without Explicit Approval:**
- [ ] URL structure / route slugs — protected
- [ ] Primary nav labels — protected
- [ ] Form field names or order — protected
- [ ] Brand logo or wordmark — protected
- [ ] Existing legal / consent / cookie copy — protected

#### C. full-output Pre-Review (Section 0.A - 0.B)

**0.A Scope Lock:**
- [ ] Full request read and understood
- [ ] Deliverable count locked: **"Delivering N deliverables:"** + list each by name
- [ ] This count is a contract — every item must appear in output

**0.B Pre-Generation Checklist (PASS GATE):**
- [ ] Full request read and understood ✓
- [ ] Deliverable count locked (N items) ✓
- [ ] All dependencies identified (packages, environment, tools) ✓
- [ ] Framework/stack confirmed from codebase or request ✓
- [ ] Output file paths confirmed ✓
- [ ] Test strategy identified ✓

#### D. frontend-review Pre-Review (Part A: A.1 - A.3)

**A.1 Scope Analysis:**
- [ ] Full request read — understand every requirement, constraint, deliverable
- [ ] All files to touch listed (components, styles, config, tests)
- [ ] Dependencies identified (packages, env setup, API contracts)
- [ ] Existing codebase checked (components, design tokens, patterns)

**A.2 Quality Plan (áp dụng đúng checks dựa trên task type):**
- [ ] Landing page → taste-skill pre-flight
- [ ] Redesign → frontend-redesign pre-audit
- [ ] Full implementation (multi-file) → full-output pre-generation
- [ ] API + UI → correctness, error handling, loading states
- [ ] Animation/motion → reduced motion, GSAP patterns, no jank
- [ ] Forms → validation, WCAG AA contrast, accessibility
- [ ] Dark mode → both modes, prefers-color-scheme, token strategy

**A.3 Pre-Review Checklist (PASS GATE):**

*Scope:*
- [ ] All deliverables listed and counted ✓
- [ ] All file paths confirmed ✓
- [ ] All dependencies identified ✓
- [ ] Framework/stack confirmed ✓

*Design (nếu UI task):*
- [ ] Design read declared ✓
- [ ] Dial values: VARIANCE / MOTION / DENSITY ✓
- [ ] Design system selected if applicable ✓
- [ ] Anti-default discipline applied ✓

*Architecture:*
- [ ] State management strategy defined ✓
- [ ] Component hierarchy planned ✓
- [ ] API integration strategy defined ✓
- [ ] Error handling strategy defined ✓
- [ ] Loading/empty/error states planned ✓

*Quality:*
- [ ] Testing strategy defined ✓
- [ ] Accessibility requirements identified ✓
- [ ] Performance budget identified ✓

#### E. security-review Pre-Review (S.1 - S.3)

**S.1 Threat Modeling:**
- [ ] Attack surface documented (untrusted inputs, external data)
- [ ] Trust boundaries identified
- [ ] Top 3 potential threats listed based on feature type
- [ ] Assets at risk assessed

**S.2 Security Requirements:**
- [ ] Authentication requirements defined
- [ ] Authorization model selected (RBAC, ABAC, ownership)
- [ ] Data classification determined
- [ ] Compliance requirements identified (GDPR, PCI-DSS, SOC2)
- [ ] Encryption requirements defined (at rest, in transit)
- [ ] Secrets storage strategy defined
- [ ] Audit logging requirements identified

**S.3 Security Design Review:**
- [ ] Input validation strategy defined
- [ ] Output encoding strategy defined
- [ ] Error handling does not leak sensitive info
- [ ] Rate limiting strategy defined
- [ ] Authentication method selected (JWT, sessions, API keys, OAuth2)
- [ ] Authorization model defined
- [ ] Secrets storage: env vars / vault / KMS decided
- [ ] Logging strategy for security events defined

**Pre-Review Checklist (PASS GATE):**
- [ ] Threat model documented ✓
- [ ] Security requirements locked ✓
- [ ] Design review PASS ✓
- [ ] Auth model defined ✓
- [ ] Secrets strategy defined ✓
- [ ] Logging strategy defined ✓

#### F. karpathy-coding Pre-Review (Overlay - Always Runs with Primary Skill)

**K.1 Think Before Coding:**
- [ ] State assumptions explicitly — what am I assuming about the request?
- [ ] If uncertain about any interpretation → STOP and ask
- [ ] If multiple valid interpretations exist → present options, don't pick silently
- [ ] If a simpler approach exists → say so, push back when warranted
- [ ] If something is unclear → stop, name what's confusing, ask

**K.2 Simplicity Check:**
- [ ] Is this over-engineered? Ask: "Would a senior engineer say this is overcomplicated?"
- [ ] No speculative features beyond what was asked
- [ ] No abstractions for single-use code
- [ ] No "flexibility" or "configurability" that wasn't requested
- [ ] No error handling for impossible scenarios
- [ ] If 200 lines can be 50 → rewrite

**K.3 Surgical Scope:**
- [ ] What MUST be changed? (list only the required changes)
- [ ] What should NOT be touched? (preserve existing code)
- [ ] Will every changed line trace directly to the user's request?
- [ ] Match existing style — don't impose personal preferences
- [ ] If unrelated dead code noticed → mention it, don't delete

**K.4 Goal Definition:**
- [ ] Success criteria defined in verifiable terms:
  - "Add validation" → "Write tests for invalid inputs, then make them pass"
  - "Fix the bug" → "Write a test that reproduces it, then make it pass"
  - "Refactor X" → "Ensure tests pass before and after"
- [ ] Multi-step plan with verification points:
  ```
  1. [Step] → verify: [check]
  2. [Step] → verify: [check]
  3. [Step] → verify: [check]
  ```

**Pre-Review Checklist (PASS GATE) - karpathy-coding Overlay:**
- [ ] Assumptions stated explicitly ✓
- [ ] No ambiguous interpretations → asked if needed ✓
- [ ] Simplicity check PASS ✓
- [ ] Scope is surgical (only required changes) ✓
- [ ] Success criteria defined ✓

